== 6.8 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The breakdown of rock in its original position is called],
  [deposition],
  [erosion],
  [transportation],
  [weathering]
)

#mcq(2, [Which of the following is a form of chemical weathering?],
  [exfoliation],
  [oxidation],
  [freeze–thaw],
  [root wedging]
)

#mcq(3, [Freeze–thaw weathering is most active in],
  [tropical rainforests],
  [coastal swamps],
  [hot deserts],
  [mountain regions with repeated freezing]
)

#mcq(4, [Exfoliation is caused mainly by],
  [plant roots],
  [repeated heating and cooling of the rock surface],
  [wind abrasion],
  [solution of limestone]
)

#mcq(5, [Carbonation is the weathering process most important in],
  [limestone regions],
  [volcanic cones],
  [sandy deserts],
  [granite uplands]
)

#mcq(6, [The slow downhill movement of soil, shown by tilted fences, is],
  [a landslide],
  [a mudflow],
  [soil creep],
  [a rockfall]
)

#mcq(7, [A barchan is formed by],
  [glacial deposition],
  [wave erosion],
  [wind deposition],
  [river deposition]
)

#mcq(8, [A yardang is produced by],
  [glacial plucking],
  [wind abrasion],
  [river erosion],
  [chemical weathering]
)

#mcq(9, [Loess is],
  [river gravel],
  [wind-blown silt],
  [volcanic ash],
  [glacial till]
)

#mcq(10, [A seif is a],
  [longitudinal dune ridge],
  [glacial valley],
  [coastal stack],
  [crescent dune]
)

#mcq(11, [A cirque is formed by],
  [wave action],
  [wind deposition],
  [river erosion at a waterfall],
  [glacial erosion at the head of a valley]
)

#mcq(12, [An arête is],
  [a rounded glacial hill],
  [a ridge of till],
  [a coastal arch],
  [a sharp ridge between two cirques]
)

#mcq(13, [A pyramidal peak forms where],
  [a dune migrates],
  [a river cuts a gorge],
  [a cliff collapses],
  [three or more cirques meet]
)

#mcq(14, [A U-shaped valley is produced by],
  [mass movement],
  [river erosion],
  [glacial erosion],
  [wind erosion]
)

#mcq(15, [A hanging valley is formed where],
  [a dune blocks a stream],
  [a tributary glacier joins a deeper main valley],
  [the sea floods a river mouth],
  [a river cuts through a ridge]
)

#mcq(16, [A drumlin is a landform of],
  [wind deposition],
  [glacial erosion],
  [coastal erosion],
  [glacial deposition]
)

#mcq(17, [A moraine is],
  [a river terrace],
  [a wave-cut platform],
  [the material deposited by a glacier],
  [a wind-eroded ridge]
)

#mcq(18, [An outwash plain is formed by],
  [wind depositing silt],
  [rivers cutting a gorge],
  [meltwater depositing sorted sand and gravel beyond the ice],
  [waves depositing shingle]
)

#mcq(19, [A roche moutonnée is],
  [a rock hump smoothed upstream and jagged downstream],
  [a coastal stack],
  [a crescent dune],
  [a limestone pavement]
)

#mcq(20, [A cliff is formed mainly by],
  [wave erosion at the base],
  [wind deposition],
  [river deposition],
  [glacial deposition]
)

#mcq(21, [A wave-cut platform is],
  [the rock shelf left as a cliff retreats],
  [a coral reef],
  [a beach of shingle],
  [a ridge of sand across a bay]
)

